{
 "analysis": "Fig 3A per-species divergence between original manuscript de novo run and RC-repaired re-run",
 "date": "2026-08-17",
 "roadmap_item": "R11 / Integrity #14",
 "root_cause": "Base-level precision in gffcompare is base-MASS weighted and is dominated by a handful of runaway predicted transcripts. gffcompare builds query exon structures from CDS *and* five_prime_UTR/three_prime_UTR features; a single blown-out UTR (or CDS) becomes one multi-Mb pseudo-exon that adds megabases of unmatched predicted bases. Because count-weighted metrics (exon/intron/intron-chain/transcript/locus level) divide by ~30,000-80,000 features, one bad transcript moves them <1 point, while base-level precision moves 13-24 points. The runaway loci differ between the original and the re-run because they are independent stochastic generations, so the divergence is species-specific and bidirectional. This is NOT a reference-version effect and NOT an RC-repair defect: both runaway transcripts examined are present in the pre-repair predictions as well.",
 "diagnostic_statistic": {
  "name": "base-mass ratio R",
  "formula": "base_Sn / base_Pr",
  "interpretation": "equals predicted exonic base mass / reference exonic base mass inside reference-bearing superloci. For one-transcript-per-locus predictions scored against a multi-isoform reference, R must be <1. R>1 is structurally impossible and flags runaway contamination.",
  "clean_range_after_filtering": "0.754 - 0.969 across all 10 species"
 },
 "runaway_definition": "predicted mRNA whose genomic span exceeds the maximum reference mRNA span in the same species test set (all reference maxima are 25,965-49,081 bp)",
 "secondary_findings": [
  "Reference/label sets differ between original and re-run for all 10 species: 9 species by -2.6% to -7.0% reference mRNAs (locus-set/annotation-version drift), Z_mays by +299% (25,123 -> 100,245 ref mRNAs; entirely different test set, tracked separately under R3).",
  "This reference drift is real but small: A_thaliana has a -4.4% reference difference and reproduces to 0.3 precision points, so reference version cannot account for 15-24 point precision swings. The original hypothesis (reference version / locus set) is NOT the cause.",
  "V_vinifera shows a genuine sensitivity divergence (base Sn 64.8 -> 60.4, exon Sn 43.3 -> 41.1) not explained by runaways; base-mass ratio is clean in both runs. Cause not determined here.",
  "gffcompare silently rejected the P_patens runaway (a 23.2 Mb three_prime_UTR whose coordinates are inconsistent with its + strand CDS) at parse time (15,050 mRNA records -> 15,049 query mRNAs), so it never entered the metric. Runaway impact is therefore erratic, not monotone.",
  "The original de novo input GFF3s are NOT archived. fig3_original/prompted/*.gff3 have the same filenames as the files named in the fig3_original/denovo/*.stats headers but are a DIFFERENT (prompted) generation - e.g. Glyma prompted query=7,986 mRNAs / ref=12,520 vs denovo header query=10,098 / ref=18,892. Only the .stats text survives for the de novo run, so original runaway transcripts can be inferred arithmetically but not enumerated."
 ],
